# 0005 - EDRAM ownership transfers between 32bpp and 64bpp targets (Gears 3 chat, 2026-10-23; base Gears2-Native 27958a8)
# Suspect for Gears 3's ch22 black squad + black ground (Gears 2 chat's 00:37 lead, confirmed in Shagg's play log
# 20261023-003356): ~476 colour tiles a frame are "unknown (colour)" = never transferred, incl. the per-object shadow
# depth D24S8 base 1440 pitch 1120 reusing tiles of k_16_16_16_16 base 1624 pitch 640/400.
# Switch: --gow2_renderer_transfer_mixed_bpp (default false = no change). On:
#   - depth target <- 64bpp colour: depth sample at 32bpp column u (after the 40-sample colour/depth swap) = half (u & 1)
#     of source pixel u >> 1 (kTransferPs t2.w);
#   - colour words between 32bpp and 64bpp colour targets, and depth -> 64bpp colour (kWordTransferPs t2.y): 32 -> 64
#     takes source columns 2u, 2u+1; 64 -> 32 takes half (u & 1) of pixel u >> 1 (Canary d3d12_render_target_cache.cc
#     ~3214-3235, ~3403);
#   - four more transfer self-tests at the first swap (8888 <-> 16_16_16_16(_FLOAT), and via D24S8).
# Checked: DXC compiles all four shader variants; index math checked against an EDRAM model (python, 0 mismatches over
# c32/c64/d32 sources and c32/c64/d32 destinations); Windows syntax check. NOT built or run. MSAA sources: not covered.
# Applies on 27958a8 with or without 0004.
diff -ruN a/src/layer0_xenos/renderer/builtin_shaders.h b/src/layer0_xenos/renderer/builtin_shaders.h
